  "narrative": "The new validation results close the main conditional PTEN inference. For H58, TP53-intact PTEN loss had discovery R42 +0.259 and independent validation R53 +0.294, strict lower bound +0.156. Under the negative raw claim direction this is stronger measured dependency and exceeds the 0.15 threshold, so I accept and close H58. For H72, the originally registered positive TP53-loss interaction with high research_signature_b is not supported; validation R79 is -0.570 with strict interval -0.965 to -0.176, entirely below the claimed positive threshold. The evidence instead supports the reversed claim H82: raw TP53-loss subgroup minus complement contrast is negative by about 0.57 to 0.78 units, and H82 is accepted because both discovery and validation strict lower bounds exceed 0.15. The practical interpretation is attenuation or possible reversal of the usual positive TP53-loss raw association in high research_signature_b lines relative to the complement, not a simple main effect. For H25, validation R80 is +0.149 with interval -0.079 to +0.376, below the claimed negative interaction threshold and unstable relative to discovery R20, so I keep the SMARCA4-loss by KEAP1-loss interaction rejected and closed. Overall, the strongest validated associations are SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger dependency, KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss associated with weaker dependency, and PTEN loss conditionally associated with stronger dependency in TP53-intact contexts. The constructed signature_b interaction is the main new supported effect, but because it uses constructed assays and an analysis-defined threshold it remains an association in this supplied dataset and is not evidence of causal biology or generalizability. The most informative next analyses are direct TP53-loss stratum effects within and outside high research_signature_b to resolve attenuation near-null versus reversal, validation of the analogous accepted H65 signature_a interaction, and conditional tests of MSI-high after removing dominant core predictor contexts.",
  "research_notes": "Current plan: H58 validated closed. H72 rejected closed; H82 validated accepted closed as the reversed TP53-by-high-signature_b interaction. H25 rejected closed; no SMARCA4 by KEAP1 interaction support. Core accepted associations: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency, KEAP1 loss weaker dependency, TP53 loss weaker dependency, PTEN loss stronger conditional TP53-intact. H65 remains accepted but not independently validated and is priority for future validation. New proposals estimate raw TP53-loss contrasts within high and low research_signature_b. If high is near null or negative, this completes signature_b interpretation; if high remains positive, the interaction may reflect attenuation less extreme. Keep H83 active for MSI-high conditional test. Lower priority: technical library/batch audits are mostly null; H73 and H74 can test signature_b modification of KEAP1/SMARCA4 if sample allocation permits."
